      "text": "To find the value of \\( y \\) given the equation \\( x^2 + x + 4 = y - 4 \\) and the value \\( x = -7 \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( x = -7 \\) into the equation \\( x^2 + x + 4 \\).\n2. Simplify the left-hand side of the equation.\n3. Solve for \\( y \\) by isolating it on one side of the equation.\n\nLet's start with the substitution:\n\n\\[ x^2 + x + 4 = (-7)^2 + (-7) + 4 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate each term:\n\n\\[ (-7)^2 = 49 \\]\n\\[ -7 = -7 \\]\n\\[ 4 = 4 \\]\n\nNow, add these values together:\n\n\\[ 49 + (-7) + 4 = 49 - 7 + 4 = 46 \\]\n\nSo, the equation \\( x^2 + x + 4 = y - 4 \\) simplifies to:\n\n\\[ 46 = y - 4 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( y \\), we add 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 46 + 4 = y \\]\n\\[ 50 = y \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
